464	     * Resolve a merchant-facing Shopify domain (custom primary domain or
465	     * raw handle) to the canonical `<handle>.myshopify.com` used by the
466	     * OAuth authorize flow.
467	     *
468	     *   mystore                     -> mystore.myshopify.com            (rewrite-only)
469	     *   mystore.myshopify.com       -> mystore.myshopify.com            (rewrite-only)
470	     *   https://mystore/admin       -> mystore.myshopify.com            (rewrite-only)
471	     *   radiorufus.com              -> <handle>.myshopify.com           (HTML discovery)
472	     *
473	     * The discovery path fetches the storefront HTML and matches a Shopify
474	     * storefront global that embeds the canonical shop URL. Most non-headless
475	     * Shopify themes still expose this — Hydrogen storefronts and heavily
476	     * stripped themes won't, so the caller must surface a clear fallback
477	     * error when we return null.
478	     *
479	     * Auth-gated (brand professionals + staff) because it lets us make
480	     * arbitrary outbound HTTP requests on behalf of the caller — an abuse
481	     * vector if left open.
482	     */
483	    public function resolveShop(Request $request): JsonResponse
484	    {
